      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Emperor of Bones can only reanimate creature cards exiled with it. Psychic Frog is the only creature among the exile targets and could be reanimated when Emperor adapts (already available for {1}{B}). Exiling Disrupting Shoal accomplishes essentially nothing - it's a non-creature and the opponent has no way to reuse it from graveyard.",
      "action_taken": "Exiled Disrupting Shoal (a non-creature instant from opponent's graveyard)",
      "better_line": "Exile Psychic Frog from own graveyard, enabling reanimation via Emperor of Bones' adapt trigger to create a hasty Psychic Frog attacker",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 130,
      "player": "MiMo Minimal",
      "decision_index": 52,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Failed to attack with a 4/4 Emperor of Bones into an empty board. The opponent has no creatures to block, so this is 4 free damage (20% of opponent's remaining life). The timeout caused the player to skip their attack entirely.",
      "action_taken": "No response — skipped the attack step without declaring any attackers.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Emperor of Bones for 4 unblockable damage, bringing the opponent from 20 to 16 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 133,
      "player": "MiMo Minimal",
      "decision_index": 53,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Player timed out and took no action with Lotus Bloom as their only mana source and no lands in play. They had castable spells that would develop their board position against an opponent's 4/4 Emperor of Bones. Lotus Bloom is a one-shot resource that was wasted this turn. Fallaji Archaeologist would have provided a blocker, milled cards for future value, and enabled Flare of Denial as free countermagic.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and passed without casting anything, wasting the Lotus Bloom turn.",
      "better_line": "Sacrifice Lotus Bloom for {U}{U}{U}, cast Fallaji Archaeologist for {1}{U} (leaving {U} open), getting a 0/3 blocker, milling 3 cards, potentially finding a spell, and enabling Flare of Denial. Alternatively, cast Tameshi for {2}{U} to develop a bigger threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 149,
      "player": "GPT52 Memoir",
      "decision_index": 58,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Fallaji Archaeologist (0/3 for 2 mana) instead of Tameshi, Reality Architect (2/3 for 3 mana) when Lotus Bloom provides exactly 3 mana. Tameshi is a bigger body (relevant blocking Emperor of Bones 4/4), uses mana more efficiently (no waste), and could potentially recur Goblin Charbelcher from graveyard later. Both serve as blue creatures for Flare of Denial.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Fallaji Archaeologist for {1}{U}, leaving 1 mana unused from Lotus Bloom",
      "better_line": "Cast Tameshi, Reality Architect for {2}{U}, using all 3 mana from Lotus Bloom efficiently, getting a bigger body and potential graveyard recursion",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 149,
      "player": "GPT52 Memoir",
      "decision_index": 58,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Emperor of Bones before casting Faithless Looting is suboptimal sequencing. Faithless Looting costs only {R} and draws 2 cards while discarding 2, providing crucial information about what's available before committing to a play. If this was the activate option (Adapt), it does nothing since the Emperor already has +1/+1 counters. If casting a second copy, the legend rule would destroy the existing 4/4 to get a fresh 2/2, losing the +1/+1 counters.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Emperor of Bones (either activating Adapt on the 4/4 or casting a second copy) before seeing Faithless Looting draws.",
      "better_line": "Cast Faithless Looting first for {R} to draw 2 cards and see more options, then decide whether to cast Emperor of Bones or take a different line based on what was drawn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 168,
      "player": "MiMo Minimal",
      "decision_index": 67,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Failed to attack with a 4/4 Emperor of Bones into an empty board, missing 4 free damage against an opponent at 16 life. The opponent has no creatures to block. This was a timeout/no response rather than a deliberate choice.",
      "action_taken": "Did not declare any attackers (timed out).",
      "better_line": "Attack with the 4/4 Emperor of Bones for 4 unblocked damage, bringing the opponent from 16 to 12 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
