      "decision_index": 74,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Disrupting Shoal was cast to counter Thoughtseize (MV 1), but with no lands in play and no blue card with MV 1 in hand, the only possible X value is 0. Disrupting Shoal with X=0 cannot counter a spell with MV 1, so this wastes the Disrupting Shoal for nothing while Thoughtseize still resolves.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Disrupting Shoal (which will have X=0) attempting to counter Thoughtseize (MV 1)",
      "better_line": "Let Thoughtseize resolve. Losing a card to Thoughtseize is bad but at least you keep Disrupting Shoal for a future spell that might have MV 0, or save it for when you have mana to hard-cast it with appropriate X value.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 207,
      "player": "GPT52 Memoir",
      "decision_index": 77,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Took Flare of Denial with Thoughtseize instead of the opponent's Goblin Charbelcher or a Whir of Invention. MiMo is the aggressor with 8 power on board vs opponent at 12 life, meaning the primary concern is the opponent comboing off with Charbelcher before being killed. Flare of Denial is less threatening since the opponent has no blue creatures to sacrifice for its alternate cost, and MiMo has almost nothing worth countering in hand (just Faithless Looting).",
      "action_taken": "Took Flare of Denial from opponent's hand",
      "better_line": "Take Goblin Charbelcher to prevent the combo kill, forcing the opponent to use Whir of Invention (requiring 7+ mana) to find another copy from the library, buying crucial time to attack for lethal.",
